course: dictionary
lesson: 267
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. Look at the words around it and what the text is about.
explain: «The Amazon giant water lily has leaves up to about three metres across.» Giant water lily, leaves and metres tell you this is about nature, so Amazon names a place: a huge river and rainforest in South America.
explain: «Every rainy season the Amazon rises by up to ten metres or more and floods huge areas of forest.» Rises and floods tell you Amazon means the river here. Always ask which meaning fits the topic best, then try it in the sentence.
explain: Amazon can also be the name of a company that sells things online, and in Greek stories the Amazons were brave women warriors. The topic of the sentence always decides which meaning you need.
fact: Amazon can mean three different things, so check the topic before you choose.
fact: «The Amazon» with «the» in front usually names the great river and rainforest in South America.
fact: Amazon can also be the name of a big online company that sells things and delivers them.
fact: In Greek stories, the Amazons were a tribe of strong women warriors.
fact: The Amazon rainforest has well over two thousand known kinds of fish, and it is being cut down, which harms nature.
exercise: «The Amazon basin has well over two thousand known kinds of fish.» What does Amazon mean here? | A big company that sells things online | A strong woman warrior from a Greek story | A kind of fish | *A huge river and rainforest in South America
exercise: Mum says, «I ordered a new book from Amazon and it came today.» What does Amazon mean? | A tall tree in the rainforest | A tribe of warriors from Greek stories | A river in South America | *A company that sells things online and delivers them
exercise: In Greek stories, the Amazons are described as fierce fighters. What were the Amazons? | Giant water lilies | A kind of frog | A rainforest in South America | *Brave women warriors
test: «Every rainy season the Amazon rises by up to ten metres and floods huge areas of forest.» What does Amazon mean here? | A warrior in a Greek story | A shop that sells books | A kind of tree | *The great river
test: In «The Amazon basin has well over two thousand known kinds of fish», which word tells you Amazon is a place? | known | fish | *basin | two thousand
exam: In «Ana ordered trainers from Amazon», what does Amazon mean? | A strong woman warrior | A river in South America | A rainforest in Asia | *A company that sells things online
